# CRM Server Node.js Express PostgreSQL - Project Rules

## Project Overview
This is a CRM server built with Node.js, Express, and PostgreSQL. The project includes both backend API services and a frontend interface.

## Code Style & Standards
- Use ES6+ JavaScript features
- Follow RESTful API design principles
- Implement proper error handling and validation
- Use async/await for asynchronous operations
- Follow the existing project structure and naming conventions

## Documentation Standards
- Keep documentation in sync with code changes
- Update README.md when adding new features or changing existing functionality
- Document API endpoints, database models, and configuration options
- Use clear and comprehensive descriptions for CRM system features

## .kiro Hooks Integration
This project uses .kiro hooks to automatically prompt for documentation updates when code changes occur. The hooks are located in `.kiro/hooks/` and will trigger when:
- JavaScript source files are modified
- Configuration files change
- Package dependencies are updated
- Database models or schemas are altered

When prompted by .kiro hooks, ensure you:
1. Analyze the code changes thoroughly
2. Update relevant documentation sections
3. Maintain consistency with existing documentation style
4. Consider the impact on API users and system administrators

## Development Workflow
- Test changes thoroughly before committing
- Update environment configuration examples if needed
- Ensure database migrations are properly documented
- Keep frontend and backend documentation synchronized

## Security & Best Practices
- Never commit sensitive information like API keys or passwords
- Use environment variables for configuration
- Implement proper authentication and authorization
- Follow security best practices for CRM data handling
